WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.770
<b>September 27th, Unified Year 1927, Eastern Front</b>

00:03.320 --> 00:07.280
<b>A promotion to general, 
disregarding the pre-war regulations...</b>

00:07.270 --> 00:11.280
With the receipt of this message, you have
been promoted to General of the Infantry

00:07.280 --> 00:10.570
<b>Stars aren't worth what they used to be.</b>

00:11.790 --> 00:15.440
<b><i>We can win incredible victories 
at the tactical level,</i></b>

00:15.440 --> 00:18.280
<b><i>and it does nothing for us strategically.</i></b>

00:18.280 --> 00:24.050
<b><i>What is Rudersdorf thinking, 
being so aggressive?</i></b>

00:26.530 --> 00:30.040
<b>I want to send a letter. 
Prepare a messenger.</b>

00:36.270 --> 00:38.650
<b>And now that the moment's here...</b>

00:38.650 --> 00:42.760
<b>I have no idea what to write.</b>

00:44.480 --> 00:45.970
<b>My friend...</b>

02:21.070 --> 02:26.620
This story is a work of fiction. People, organizations, locations, laws, names, etc. have no relation to any real-life counterparts.

02:30.100 --> 02:32.240
<b>There's no time...</b>

02:32.630 --> 02:34.940
<b>We're running out of time...</b>

02:35.590 --> 02:38.590
<b>Episode Eleven
Hourglass</b>

02:47.560 --> 02:50.710
<b>What's wrong? What happened?</b>

02:51.130 --> 02:54.070
<b>They're evacuating the area around 
the southern border, they say.</b>

02:54.750 --> 02:57.890
<b>You don't know what was in 
the military's official paper?</b>

02:58.970 --> 03:01.870
<b>Oh, you're right.</b>

03:05.800 --> 03:08.110
<b>It's been a whole year, huh?</b>

03:09.640 --> 03:11.190
<b>I'm sorry.</b>

03:11.620 --> 03:13.490
<b>Please don't apologize.</b>

03:13.910 --> 03:18.090
<b>We were only married for five days, 
but I have no regrets.</b>

03:18.090 --> 03:19.000
<b>And...</b>

03:19.640 --> 03:21.620
<b>I was blessed with my child.</b>

03:22.820 --> 03:27.600
<b>Before he left that day, he said...</b>

03:27.600 --> 03:32.280
<b>If something happened... 
if he died for me, for us...</b>

03:34.710 --> 03:37.230
<b>then his death meant something.</b>

03:45.110 --> 03:47.920
<b>You who have volunteered</b>

03:47.920 --> 03:52.780
<b>despite being ineligible for conscription 
are the chosen ones of the Empire,</b>

03:52.680 --> 03:55.080
<b>Such wonderful patriotism.</b>

03:52.780 --> 03:55.090
<b>its pride, and its future!</b>

03:55.340 --> 03:59.200
<b>Our home is in danger! 
But we have no need to fear!</b>

03:55.660 --> 03:59.090
<b>Sheesh... I can't believe there 
are people who don't volunteer.</b>

03:59.090 --> 04:00.870
<b>I can't wait to see 
the looks on their faces</b>

03:59.200 --> 04:02.860
<b>For you will be among our ranks!</b>

04:00.870 --> 04:03.560
<b>when they try to join the 
government after the war.</b>

04:02.860 --> 04:07.840
<b>Those who come after you 
will sing of your bravery!</b>

04:03.560 --> 04:04.890
<b>That's right.</b>

04:04.890 --> 04:09.060
<b>What use are they, when everyone 
else is sacrificing themselves?</b>

04:09.720 --> 04:13.020
<b><i>In the face of this... these voices...</i></b>

04:13.020 --> 04:16.150
<b><i>Can we say that it was all for nothing?</i></b>

04:27.620 --> 04:31.120
<b>Low-altitude bombing?
 In broad daylight? Impossible!</b>

04:36.020 --> 04:37.370
<b>What's the situation?</b>

04:37.370 --> 04:39.910
<b>General, it's bad.</b>

04:39.910 --> 04:42.670
<b>They've bombed our ceremonial grounds.</b>

04:42.670 --> 04:44.540
<b>The damage was minimal, but...</b>

04:44.540 --> 04:47.710
<b>It's humiliating for the army, yes.</b>

04:47.710 --> 04:51.620
<b>They've used their new high-speed bombers.</b>

04:51.620 --> 04:53.860
<b>Our interceptors couldn't make it in time.</b>

04:53.860 --> 04:58.730
<b>Lightweight fighters couldn't catch up 
to bombers carrying bombs?</b>

04:58.730 --> 05:04.290
<b>The enemy's high cruising speed means 
there's little time to intercept them.</b>

05:04.290 --> 05:06.100
<b>And when there's a small number of them,</b>

05:06.100 --> 05:08.450
<b>it's difficult to identify 
and track them, I'm told.</b>

05:10.170 --> 05:14.400
<b>So why were we bombed before 
we could even get an alert out?</b>

05:14.400 --> 05:17.050
<b>They've been having 
a small number of bombers</b>

05:17.050 --> 05:20.080
<b>serve as a decoy to distract 
our interceptor units.</b>

05:20.340 --> 05:22.990
<b>This was likely judged to be 
another decoy and ignored.</b>

05:22.990 --> 05:28.100
<b>We tried not to be the boy who cried wolf,
 but the wolf was really there?</b>

05:28.100 --> 05:31.220
<b>We'll have to hurry and research 
a way to deal with this.</b>

05:31.220 --> 05:33.410
<b>The enemy is coming up 
with new ideas constantly.</b>

05:33.410 --> 05:35.820
<b>We can't fall behind!</b>

05:35.820 --> 05:37.000
<b>Sir!</b>

05:40.190 --> 05:41.320
<b><i>That's right.</i></b>

05:41.710 --> 05:44.080
<b><i>We can't fall behind.</i></b>

05:44.080 --> 05:47.020
<b><i>We... the Empire...</i></b>

05:47.530 --> 05:50.390
<b><i>cannot fall behind!</i></b>

06:05.710 --> 06:07.500
<b><i>It can't end yet.</i></b>

06:12.050 --> 06:15.570
<b><i>That idiot Zettour isn't 
going to like this at all.</i></b>

06:16.430 --> 06:21.170
<b><i>But it's better than 
missing our chance...</i></b>

06:21.170 --> 06:22.270
<b><i>We must do it now!</i></b>

06:22.270 --> 06:26.780
War Plan: Ildoa

06:23.400 --> 06:25.860
<b><i>For the Empire!</i></b>

06:32.780 --> 06:35.790
<b>September 30th, Unified Year 1927</b>

06:43.590 --> 06:46.790
<b>You came all the way out here?</b>

06:47.160 --> 06:49.520
<b>You must have really missed me.</b>

06:50.350 --> 06:52.030
<b>I won't deny it.</b>

06:52.640 --> 06:55.190
<b>It was a joke...</b>

06:55.190 --> 06:57.150
<b>You read the plan, I assume.</b>

06:57.150 --> 07:00.570
<b>Yes. And I have a question.</b>

07:01.050 --> 07:03.650
<b>Have you gone mad?</b>

07:03.900 --> 07:05.470
<b>Of course not.</b>

07:05.470 --> 07:08.150
<b>I'm trying to win victory for our Empire.</b>

07:08.930 --> 07:12.190
<b>Securing air superiority to the west,</b>

07:12.510 --> 07:15.310
<b>ensuring our ability to continue the war,</b>

07:15.310 --> 07:16.730
<b>and then taking down Ildoa.</b>

07:17.070 --> 07:19.490
<b>It's the only way to win.</b>

07:20.770 --> 07:22.490
<b>A wonderful plan.</b>

07:22.490 --> 07:27.000
<b>Except for the fact that 
it's utterly impossible.</b>

07:28.510 --> 07:33.810
<b>If the military takes complete control, 
it will be possible.</b>

07:33.810 --> 07:35.780
<b>We can truly put our all into this.</b>

07:36.500 --> 07:40.550
<b>The military has the ability, 
the resolve, and the willingness!</b>

07:40.550 --> 07:42.550
<b>So we can do it!</b>

07:42.550 --> 07:45.270
<b>We were going to try to 
resolve this through diplomacy.</b>

07:45.270 --> 07:48.400
<b>Hadn't you agreed to that?</b>

07:48.400 --> 07:50.900
<b>That's already failed.</b>

07:50.900 --> 07:52.130
<b>Don't be stupid.</b>

07:52.130 --> 07:53.410
<b>We can make it work.</b>

07:53.410 --> 07:56.490
<b>You think we can make those 
ridiculous conditions work?</b>

07:56.970 --> 08:01.420
<b>We got them interested enough that 
they're willing to give us conditions.</b>

08:01.760 --> 08:03.160
<b>Then...</b>

08:03.380 --> 08:08.000
<b>If we both lose another million, 
no, ten million lives,</b>

08:08.000 --> 08:11.550
<b>even the stupidest of them 
will be willing to talk.</b>

08:12.200 --> 08:13.290
<b>Don't be ridiculous!</b>

08:13.290 --> 08:15.600
<b>Do you know how many have already died?</b>

08:16.050 --> 08:20.400
<b>What's the point of more soldiers 
dying needless deaths?</b>

08:20.400 --> 08:23.090
<b>Looks like there's still 
some sanity left in you.</b>

08:23.090 --> 08:26.250
<b>But you're giving up on diplomacy?</b>

08:26.250 --> 08:29.520
<b>The more time passes, 
the harder diplomacy becomes.</b>

08:29.520 --> 08:33.790
<b>The Empire still can gain 
tactical superiority.</b>

08:33.790 --> 08:37.950
<b>But if more time passes, 
we'll lose that as well!</b>

08:37.950 --> 08:40.270
<b>So this is your plan?</b>

08:40.270 --> 08:42.450
<b>"Hit them while we still can?"</b>

08:42.450 --> 08:43.370
<b>Indeed.</b>

08:43.370 --> 08:44.240
<b>This can't work.</b>

08:44.240 --> 08:47.060
<b>Sacrificing the strategic 
for the tactical...</b>

08:47.060 --> 08:49.500
<b>We can't be pushed
 any more onto the back foot.</b>

08:50.270 --> 08:52.580
<b>We need to do something drastic!</b>

08:56.910 --> 09:01.060
<b>And you call yourself a strategy officer?</b>

09:01.060 --> 09:02.230
<b>What?</b>

09:02.230 --> 09:06.420
<b>Why are you drooling just 
because someone rang a bell?</b>

09:06.420 --> 09:08.880
<b>When did you become a mere dog?</b>

09:08.880 --> 09:10.000
<b>Shut up!</b>

09:10.000 --> 09:13.060
<b>If words won't make them 
understand, then force...</b>

09:13.580 --> 09:16.410
<b>Look at reality, Rudersdorf!</b>

09:16.410 --> 09:18.500
<b>You've gone crazy!</b>

09:18.500 --> 09:19.790
<b>No, you have!</b>

09:19.790 --> 09:21.340
<b>Is that head on your 
shoulders just for show?</b>

09:21.340 --> 09:22.990
<b>What is that brain of yours for?</b>

09:22.990 --> 09:25.040
<b>Think about this rationally!</b>

09:27.280 --> 09:29.420
<b>We cannot lose this!</b>

09:29.420 --> 09:34.870
<b>What do we say to the Empire if we can't 
bring a victory worth the sacrifices?</b>

09:36.900 --> 09:38.760
<b>We say just one thing.</b>

09:39.530 --> 09:43.010
<b>We apologize for our incompetence.</b>

09:44.740 --> 09:47.260
<b>Then we let them stone us to death.</b>

09:57.170 --> 10:03.740
<b>Zettour, use your head before 
you start spouting nonsense.</b>

10:04.020 --> 10:06.420
<b>We're Imperial soldiers!</b>

10:06.840 --> 10:09.100
<b>Defeat may be inevitable,</b>

10:09.530 --> 10:12.280
<b>but we still have to win!</b>

10:15.040 --> 10:18.110
<b>Use my head, huh?</b>

10:19.050 --> 10:23.700
<b>Sheesh... It's tough having 
an idiot for a friend.</b>

10:23.700 --> 10:29.150
<b>If I wanted to, I could use my 
authority as general to shut you up.</b>

10:30.530 --> 10:33.190
<b>Shall I be more formal when 
I speak with you, then?</b>

10:33.190 --> 10:34.550
<b>Don't bother.</b>

10:34.550 --> 10:37.790
<b>I'm sure you got a promotion, too.</b>

10:37.790 --> 10:40.200
<b>You hear fast.</b>

10:40.750 --> 10:46.500
<b>I never thought we'd both be 
wearing these cheap stars.</b>

10:46.500 --> 10:48.170
<b>I'm sure.</b>

10:48.170 --> 10:51.790
<b>Regiment Commander Laudon 
must be quite surprised.</b>

10:51.790 --> 10:56.050
<b>He might get so excited, he starts 
playing a tune on the wake-up bugle.</b>

11:00.940 --> 11:03.900
<b>I can see how firm you are about this.</b>

11:03.900 --> 11:07.640
<b>As your friend, I'll do all I can.</b>

11:08.050 --> 11:10.520
<b>Thanks... I owe you one.</b>

11:23.130 --> 11:24.890
<b>Excuse me.</b>

11:27.080 --> 11:30.620
<b>Was General Rudersdorf doing well?</b>

11:31.800 --> 11:34.840
<b>Yes, same as ever.</b>

11:35.170 --> 11:37.830
<b>Death itself couldn't change him.</b>

11:38.210 --> 11:40.510
<b>I'm glad to hear that.</b>

11:40.510 --> 11:44.300
<b>So, what can I do for you?</b>

11:44.820 --> 11:48.750
<b>Lieutenant Colonel, I need you 
to do something for me.</b>

11:49.090 --> 11:50.380
<b>Of course.</b>

11:50.380 --> 11:52.320
<b>What is it?</b>

11:54.180 --> 11:56.930
<b>I want you...</b>

11:58.270 --> 12:00.460
<b>...to kill my best friend.</b>

12:11.750 --> 12:14.490
<b>What did you say, sir?</b>

12:14.490 --> 12:18.510
<b>I want you to blow 
my best friend's brains out.</b>

12:18.900 --> 12:20.800
<b>I believe I was quite clear.</b>

12:22.360 --> 12:24.140
<b>May I ask why?</b>

12:24.140 --> 12:27.510
<b>Oh? You'd like to hear the reason?</b>

12:27.510 --> 12:30.820
<b>I'm not a murderer 
who kills without reason.</b>

12:30.820 --> 12:33.890
<b>I am a soldier who knows her duties 
and values her honor.</b>

12:34.210 --> 12:39.890
<b>He said he's gonna flip over something</b>

12:39.890 --> 12:43.030
<b>that must remain where it is.</b>

12:43.030 --> 12:48.440
<b>Even military logic can never be 
put above the national interest.</b>

12:48.840 --> 12:51.650
<b>The strategic serving the tactical?</b>

12:51.650 --> 12:53.230
<b>That can't happen.</b>

12:53.460 --> 12:58.150
<b>At the tactical level,
I will gladly seek victory.</b>

12:58.150 --> 13:03.280
<b>But that's only possible 
if the Empire has a national strategy.</b>

13:03.280 --> 13:04.910
<b>Tactics with no strategy?</b>

13:04.910 --> 13:06.750
<b>Victory with no way to make use of it?</b>

13:06.750 --> 13:09.440
<b>Anything we accomplish like that 
is completely meaningless.</b>

13:09.950 --> 13:12.890
<b>Let me ask one question.</b>

13:13.320 --> 13:16.060
<b>What will you do once 
this is accomplished?</b>

13:16.060 --> 13:19.820
<b>We'll need to prepare for a clean exit.</b>

13:20.040 --> 13:24.440
<b>You're not opposed to 
the military taking full control?</b>

13:24.440 --> 13:28.450
<b>Indeed. But if we're too 
forceful when we do it,</b>

13:28.450 --> 13:31.150
<b>we'll only bring about 
the Empire's downfall.</b>

13:31.150 --> 13:34.530
<b>We need to avoid chaos, 
no matter how this ends.</b>

13:40.950 --> 13:42.360
<b>Lieutenant Colonel.</b>

13:44.240 --> 13:45.400
<b>Do it.</b>

13:47.800 --> 13:51.660
<b>Make Rudersdorf a field marshal.</b>

14:01.900 --> 14:04.190
<b>This is absurd.</b>

14:07.950 --> 14:12.060
<b>Kill him because he's in your way?
That's unthinkable.</b>

14:12.060 --> 14:14.410
<b>Absolutely out of the question.</b>

14:14.410 --> 14:16.670
<b>It's a necessary sacrifice.</b>

14:16.670 --> 14:19.710
<b>Even now, you don't want to kill an ally?</b>

14:20.050 --> 14:22.680
<b>Yes. I'm sorry...</b>

14:22.680 --> 14:26.960
<b>But you seem to be debating 
entirely the wrong question.</b>

14:26.960 --> 14:28.290
<b>What?</b>

14:28.810 --> 14:31.590
<b>You really don't understand?</b>

14:31.590 --> 14:33.670
<b>That's a shame.</b>

14:34.560 --> 14:38.320
<b>Sir, humans are a valuable resource.</b>

14:38.320 --> 14:41.020
<b>They shouldn't be killed for nothing.</b>

14:41.960 --> 14:46.230
<b>If you simply kill General Rudersdorf, 
then his death is worth nothing.</b>

14:46.230 --> 14:51.230
<b>A high-ranking officer should die 
in a way that's more useful.</b>

14:52.080 --> 14:55.990
<b>For instance, they could die</b>

14:56.590 --> 14:59.520
<b>as the head of a treasonous plot 
to install a military dictatorship.</b>

15:00.330 --> 15:01.650
<b>I see.</b>

15:01.650 --> 15:05.310
<b>We don't simply deem him 
a cancer and eliminate him?</b>

15:05.310 --> 15:06.300
<b>Yes.</b>

15:06.300 --> 15:10.780
<b>His death could be the trigger
 for a selective purge of the army.</b>

15:10.780 --> 15:12.650
<b>And the danger such a plot would pose</b>

15:12.650 --> 15:15.430
<b>gives us an excuse to take 
full military control of the war.</b>

15:15.980 --> 15:19.440
<b>What you're proposing 
sounds like a coup to me.</b>

15:19.440 --> 15:22.120
<b>I believe it could be done legally.</b>

15:22.120 --> 15:27.430
<b>A single company of MPs would be enough 
to arrest anyone we deemed his accomplice.</b>

15:27.870 --> 15:30.000
<b>And then we could do whatever we wanted.</b>

15:32.430 --> 15:36.440
<b>And how would you kick this off?</b>

15:36.790 --> 15:42.070
<b>The best thing to tell the public is
that he suffered an accidental death.</b>

15:42.070 --> 15:45.900
<b>Ideally, we find evidence of a plot 
when searching through his belongings,</b>

15:45.900 --> 15:47.950
<b>and then begin the purge.</b>

15:48.280 --> 15:49.640
<b>Not bad.</b>

15:49.640 --> 15:51.170
<b>No, it's perfect.</b>

15:51.170 --> 15:55.470
<b>There's just one problem.</b>

15:55.850 --> 15:57.220
<b>Yes, sir.</b>

15:57.220 --> 16:03.880
<b>This plan needs someone with the resolve 
to take full military control of the war.</b>

16:06.670 --> 16:08.560
<b>I'm abandoning my friend.</b>

16:09.320 --> 16:13.460
<b>I'll have to reserve 
a seat for myself in hell.</b>

16:18.370 --> 16:19.640
<b>Very well.</b>

16:19.640 --> 16:22.470
<b>I'll begin my plan, then.</b>

16:22.470 --> 16:24.570
<b>How do we get rid of him?</b>

16:24.570 --> 16:27.210
<b>How about a plane accident?</b>

16:27.210 --> 16:29.790
<b>A rare event that's 
actually quite frequent.</b>

16:29.790 --> 16:35.790
<b>Yes. Since the war started, 
we've been short on parts and mechanics.</b>

16:35.790 --> 16:40.920
<b>And I'll send my mages 
to make sure it happens.</b>

16:42.170 --> 16:43.680
<b>You'll sacrifice the plane,</b>

16:43.680 --> 16:47.630
<b>as well as the reputation 
of those who were there?</b>

16:47.980 --> 16:50.760
<b>I feel terrible about it.</b>

16:50.760 --> 16:54.200
<b>But sir, if I may...</b>

16:54.450 --> 16:57.280
<b>You seem to be grinning.</b>

16:59.530 --> 17:03.880
<b>Lieutenant Colonel, I'm asking 
a lot of you and your men.</b>

17:04.790 --> 17:06.190
<b>You always do.</b>

17:06.190 --> 17:08.960
<b>Yeah, you always do.</b>

17:08.960 --> 17:10.210
<b>Very good.</b>

17:10.210 --> 17:13.580
<b>Then let us shed the blood 
that must be shed.</b>

17:13.850 --> 17:14.510
<b>Yes, sir.</b>

17:15.200 --> 17:17.710
<b>I'll have good news for you soon.</b>

17:27.480 --> 17:32.480
<b>Eastern Front Multinational Volunteer Army Garrison</b>

17:27.970 --> 17:30.690
<b>You're serious about this, Uncle?</b>

17:30.690 --> 17:32.480
<b>Impressive, isn't it?</b>

17:33.060 --> 17:37.020
<b>Shuttle bombers that leave the Kingdom 
and land in the Federation.</b>

17:37.020 --> 17:42.050
<b>An ultra-long range bombing that can 
put even more stress on the Empire.</b>

17:42.050 --> 17:45.940
<b>On the surface, 
it's a major strategic offensive.</b>

17:45.940 --> 17:47.960
<b>No one's going to suspect</b>

17:47.960 --> 17:52.350
<b>it's actually just a decoy to cover an 
attempt to assassinate an Imperial VIP.</b>

17:52.350 --> 17:57.000
<b>We can't let the Empire start asking 
where the information came from.</b>

17:57.000 --> 18:00.030
<b>A spy in the heart of the Empire, was it?</b>

18:00.030 --> 18:03.670
<b>It's fine to keep secrets, 
but you're asking a lot of the soldiers.</b>

18:03.670 --> 18:08.770
<b>But General Rudersdorf's head is worth it.</b>

18:09.970 --> 18:13.790
<b>And so I wanted to ask a favor.</b>

18:13.790 --> 18:18.570
<b>I don't want our enemies, or even 
our friends, suspecting anything.</b>

18:18.790 --> 18:21.480
<b>So you want him dead without 
the Federation finding out?</b>

18:21.880 --> 18:24.950
<b>I'll ask you to do 
what it takes to cover it up.</b>

18:25.300 --> 18:27.640
<b>Now, I'll be going.</b>

18:27.640 --> 18:28.330
<b>Hey—</b>

18:28.330 --> 18:31.460
<b>Same Day • Federation Garrison</b>

18:29.060 --> 18:30.610
<b>A shuttle bombing?</b>

18:30.610 --> 18:31.460
<b>Yes.</b>

18:31.700 --> 18:36.200
<b>Allied Kingdom bombers will strike 
the Empire and land on Federation soil.</b>

18:36.200 --> 18:40.380
<b>They'll resupply and return to the Kingdom
 while doing another bombing run.</b>

18:40.380 --> 18:43.540
<b>Both countries will work together 
to attack the Empire.</b>

18:43.540 --> 18:45.690
<b>An example of international friendship.</b>

18:45.690 --> 18:48.310
<b>International friendship 
is a wonderful thing.</b>

18:48.310 --> 18:51.890
<b>So, what does the party want from me?</b>

18:51.890 --> 18:55.070
<b>We want you to be prepared 
to welcome our friends.</b>

18:55.070 --> 18:59.690
<b>So we're to guide the bombers 
to the base and protect them?</b>

18:59.690 --> 19:00.910
<b>Understood.</b>

19:00.910 --> 19:05.030
<b>Comrade Colonel, the Federation 
is planning a little surprise</b>

19:05.030 --> 19:07.080
<b>for our friends after their long trip.</b>

19:07.080 --> 19:08.450
<b>A surprise?</b>

19:08.450 --> 19:09.500
<b>For instance,</b>

19:11.390 --> 19:14.670
<b>ace mages equipped with 
a new type of computation jewel.</b>

19:14.670 --> 19:18.920
<b>How about surprising them with a much 
better escort than they expected?</b>

19:19.200 --> 19:23.820
<b><i>So we need to show them our strength 
before they start looking down on us?</i></b>

19:24.740 --> 19:29.170
<b><i>With these new, unstable
 computation jewels? That won't be easy.</i></b>

19:29.170 --> 19:30.050
<b>But...</b>

19:30.510 --> 19:34.780
<b>If that's what the party wants, 
of course I'll do it.</b>

19:35.160 --> 19:37.420
<b>Let's show off this new jewel.</b>

19:38.780 --> 19:41.110
<b>October 3rd, Unified Year 1927</b>

19:41.840 --> 19:43.980
<b>You're really sure about this, right?</b>

19:45.600 --> 19:46.480
<b>Sir?</b>

19:47.310 --> 19:49.080
<b>Just give me a moment.</b>

19:49.610 --> 19:51.380
<b>He's a friend.</b>

19:51.720 --> 19:55.620
<b>A part of me thinks 
there's still time to talk him down.</b>

19:56.770 --> 20:00.800
<b>It seems I'm not as cold-hearted 
as I thought I was.</b>

20:01.420 --> 20:05.280
<b>If I may, sir, we're all human.</b>

20:06.280 --> 20:08.330
<b>That's surprising, Lieutenant Colonel.</b>

20:08.330 --> 20:10.730
<b>Are you human?</b>

20:10.730 --> 20:12.910
<b>Of course I am.</b>

20:12.910 --> 20:17.360
<b>If a god or a devil 
wants to get in my way,</b>

20:17.360 --> 20:22.530
<b>I strongly feel it is my task 
to crush them with human might.</b>

20:23.130 --> 20:26.020
<b>I see. But...</b>

20:26.460 --> 20:30.670
<b>I've burnt away any humanity I had.</b>

21:08.590 --> 21:11.320
<b>I'm sorry, but I need 
you to do something.</b>

21:50.000 --> 21:54.880
<b><i>You always get one last shit job 
to do before you quit.</i></b>

21:54.880 --> 21:57.440
<b><i>But if I want to make a clean exit...</i></b>

22:00.180 --> 22:02.120
<b><i>I have no choice.</i></b>

22:06.010 --> 22:10.010
<b>Next Time
Exit</b>
